  "name": "Ranger Adaptation: the strongest Footpad's and Woodsman's Adaptation wins per target, any caster…",
  "contract": [
    "Footpad's Adaptation (523489, ranks 523490-523493) and Greater Footpad's Adaptation 523513 grant armor",
    "(SPELL_AURA_MOD_RESISTANCE) and all primary attributes (SPELL_AURA_MOD_STAT); rank 5 523493 and 523513",
    "both grant 285 armor and 12 of each attribute, and the single-target tooltip says 'Does not stack with",
    "other similar effects'. Woodsman's Adaptation (800266, ranks up to 803666) and Greater Woodsman's",
    "Adaptation 680294 grant melee and ranged attack power; rank 7 803666 and 680294 both grant 232.",
    "spell_group 2100002 (523489, 523513) and 2100003 (800266, 680294) with",
    "SPELL_GROUP_STACK_RULE_EXCLUSIVE_HIGHEST (4) make each pair one buff per target:",
    "Unit::IsHighestExclusiveAuraEffect refuses a weaker cast, an equal or stronger cast replaces the older",
    "one whoever cast it, and the two pairs stay independent. Rule 1 (EXCLUSIVE) would let a rank 1 cast",
    "(523489: 105 armor, 4 of each attribute; 800266: 30 attack power) replace a raid member's Greater buff.",
    "Expected on a grouped warrior ally: max-rank Footpad's from one Ranger gives +309 armor (285 plus 2",
    "armor per point of its +12 Agility); Greater Footpad's from a second Ranger replaces it (still +309, not",
    "+618); the first Ranger's max rank replaces the Greater again; the second Ranger's copy of the same rank",
    "replaces the first Ranger's; Woodsman's rank 7 (+232 attack power over the Footpad's-buffed value) sits",
    "beside Footpad's, and Greater Woodsman's replaces it (still +232) without touching Footpad's. A rank 1",
    "Footpad's or Woodsman's cast on a target carrying the Greater buff is refused and leaves the Greater",
    "buff and the stat totals unchanged; with the Greater buff removed, rank 1 lands, and a Greater cast then",
    "replaces it.",
    "Ranger Adaptation: the strongest Footpad's and Woodsman's Adaptation wins per target, any caster (#5000,",
    "#5011)"
  ],
